    "turn_idx": 79,
    "turn_text": "right? So for them to hide behind the First Amendment is a bit disingenuous. But secondly, even if you apply the First Amendment principles, which is that you want freedom of speech, there are a lot of limitations to that principle. For example, you can't incite violence under the First Amendment. You can't yell fire in a crowded theater. You have to be, and we want to have speech that is actually helping deliberation and responsible decision-making. So there are philosophers who have written about this. You're going to compromise with communicative action. His whole work is about what are the rules of speech that are actually going to lead to the truth and better outcomes. And what I would do if I were a Jack Dorsey is to acknowledge that just having a platform where people can express whatever comes to their",
